\b\f43\fs24\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\fs24\lang9\langfe8192\langnp9\insrsid8141396 \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
Differentiate between push and pull strategies for promotion.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs24\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 Ans 51) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f43\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
A push strategy is when a company proactively and aggressively markets or promotes a product or product line to the market place or a market segment. This can be through cold calling, di\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
rect mail, sending email blasts, advertising, etc. in which the company explicitly asks a prospective consumer to take action such as: \line "Buy Now!" "Call Today" Sign Up Now" "For More Info Visit..."\line 
Some times push strategy is accompanied by a sense of urg\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 e\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 ncy and limited time offers and one-time incentives to prompt consumers' immediate action.
\par \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43  
\par \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
On the other hand a pull strategy is more passive than aggressive. In this case companies may have longer term strategy in mind. A company may look to instill top of mind awareness in the marketplace or build its Brand equity. Another twist to pull offers
,\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
 is FREE Offers, this is when prospects are offered free trials, free information passively. The purpose behind this is to generate leads to which marketers can later promote back-end offers, in fact sometimes marketers will lose money upfront because the
\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 y\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43  know they'll make up their money in the back-end. Good examples are: Coke Commercials (Enjoy Coca, Polar, Polar Bears) Lexus Commercials, Free Offers on the internet or ON TV.
\par \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43  To summarize a push strategy is aggressive, direct and calls prospects to acti\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 on. A pull strategy is passive, instills a message for top of mind awareness or to build Brand equity.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs24\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 
\par \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43     }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\fs24\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 
\par \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 Question No: 52    ( Marks: 5 ) 
