\b\f43\fs24\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43  Define channel of communication, discuss different types of channels of business communication.
\par 
\par \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 Ans 53) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
Various sources used by marketers to send marketing messages to potential consumers. Communication channels may be personal, involvin\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
g two or more persons communicating directly with each other, such as a customer/salesperson relationship, or impersonal such as bill boards etc.
\par \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43  Types of communications:
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li450\ri0\sb100\sa240\nowidctlpar\tx720\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin450\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 \loch\af43\dbch\af31505\hich\f43 \'b7\tab }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 Verbal Communication}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 
\line \line \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 Verbal communication is further divided into written and or\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
al communication. The oral communication refers to the spoken words in the communication process. Oral communication can either be face-to-face communication or a conversation over the phone or on the voice chat over the Internet. Spoken conversations or 
\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 d\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
ialogs are influenced by voice modulation, pitch, volume and even the speed and clarity of speaking. The other type of verbal communication is written communication. Written communication can be either via snail mail, or email. The effectiveness of writte
\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 n\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43  communication depends on the style of writing, vocabulary used, grammar, clarity and precision of language. 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li450\ri0\sb100\sa100\nowidctlpar\tx720\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin450\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 \loch\af43\dbch\af31505\hich\f43 \'b7\tab }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 Nonverbal Communication}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 
\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43  \line \line Non-verbal communication includes the overall body language of the person who is speaking, which will include the body\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
 posture, the hand gestures, and overall body movements. The facial expressions also play a major role while communication since the expressions on a person\hich\f43 \rquote \loch\f43 
s face say a lot about his/her mood. On the other hand gestures like a handshake, a smile or a hug\hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43  \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
can independently convey emotions. Non verbal communication can also be in the form of pictorial representations, signboards, or even photographs
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\fs24\cf22\lang1033\langfe8192\langnp1033\insrsid8141396 \\
